Description: A workflow to map the risk of chemicals for wildlife: habitat,
  food web, dispersal, exposure and risk. Starting from a raster of chemical
  concentrations in the environment (e.g., metals in soil, pesticides in
  fields), the package builds habitat layers for a set of species, organises
  them in a directed acyclic graph representing a food web, and propagates
  the flow of elements (e.g., food, energy, chemicals) along its links. It
  also provides soil interpolation by kriging, dispersal by kernel
  convolution or by circuit theory (through the optional 'Julia' package
  'Omniscape'), land cover retrieval for France ('OCS-GE') and Europe
  ('EUNIS'), and Bayesian calibration of transfer models with 'Stan'.
